;; Allowlist for `bb check:no-boundary` (BOU-209 rename gate).
;;
;; Repo-relative path PREFIXES exempt from the residual-boundary scan. These
;; legitimately keep "boundary" tokens: history, planning docs, and the rename
;; tooling itself. Extend as genuine exceptions surface during the rename; do
;; NOT add real source here to silence the gate.
;;
;; Every entry needs a reason, and every entry must be individually
;; load-bearing: the gate audits this list on each run and fails on an entry
;; whose path is gone, that suppresses nothing, or that is already covered by
;; another entry. A prefix that matches nothing is silent by construction — it
;; cannot announce that it stopped working.
;;
;; CHANGELOG.md, docs/superpowers/, .wagoe/ and scripts/rename_wagoe.clj are
;; deliberately absent: they are baked into `default-allow-paths` in the gate
;; itself. Repeating them here changed nothing and the audit now says so.
{:allow-paths
 [;; Doc-drift linter: its #"boundary\.<ns>" pattern matches ns references in
  ;; the docs it lints. Only the dev/ copy carries the pattern — scripts/
  ;; became a thin shim over this namespace in #344 and needs no exemption.
  "dev/wagoe/tools/docs_lint.clj"
  ;; Clojars relocation tooling (BOU-218). Same category as the rename tooling
  ;; above: the retired org.boundary-app coordinates and the boundary-cli /
  ;; boundary-mcp artifact ids are its SUBJECT, not residue. It publishes the
  ;; stubs that point those coordinates at com.wagoe, so it cannot name them
  ;; any other way. Permanent — the retired group stays dormant, not deleted.
  "libs/tools/src/wagoe/tools/relocate.clj"
  "libs/tools/test/wagoe/tools/relocate_test.clj"
  ;; Publishing guide: its "Retired coordinates" section documents the same
  ;; relocation. Whole-file exemption because the allowlist matches on path
  ;; prefix only — when editing the rest of this file, note the gate is blind
  ;; to it and check old coordinates by hand.
  "dev-docs/reference/publishing.adoc"]}
